{"id": 77, "ts": 1780423304.6604102, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is our strongest option. As Sarah highlighted, his ability to make correct decisions quickly, stay calm in a crisis, and understand complicated technology directly addresses the core pilot criteria of decision quality, stress resilience, and technical competence. While he does struggle with communicating ideas, is seen as egocentric, and is not eager to pursue further education, these issues are less detrimental than the interpersonal problems we see with Candidate\u202fB\u2014specifically his nasty remarks toward colleagues and a weak memory for numbers, which could jeopardize crew cooperation and attention to detail. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, the capacity to make rapid, accurate decisions under pressure outweighs the relatively milder communication shortcomings of Candidate\u202fC, especially since his technical grasp is solid. Therefore, I continue to vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
